      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 108.08,
      "end_seconds": 113.04,
      "duration_seconds": 4.96,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.2,
      "end_seconds": 119.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.09,
      "text": "tell me about your work"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.67,
      "end_seconds": 125.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.18,
      "text": "I'm a software engineer, so I'm at a screen all day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.82,
      "end_seconds": 128.52,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "alright how about exercise?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 129.86,
      "end_seconds": 133.76,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Not really, I don't get much exercise."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 147.04,
      "end_seconds": 152.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.98,
      "text": "Alright anyone in the the family with similar problems or other conditions?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.67,
      "end_seconds": 159.35,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "my father had a heart attack yeah, my uncle had colon cancer"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.59,
      "end_seconds": 164.91,
      "duration_seconds": 4.32,
      "text": "let's go through your medication what are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 166.24,
      "end_seconds": 170.43,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "I take losartan, 50 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 171.17,
      "end_seconds": 179.69,
      "duration_seconds": 8.52,
      "text": "she is supposed to take it once a day, but I can't say she always does"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.87,
      "end_seconds": 195.83,
      "duration_seconds": 14.96,
      "text": "I take metformin 500 milligrams twice a day for my sugar. Iron tablets. I take it once a day. I'd been on telmisartan not any more though I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.12,
      "end_seconds": 204.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.83,
      "text": "what about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 206.5,
      "end_seconds": 210.85,
      "duration_seconds": 4.35,
      "text": "I've, I've got high blood pressure. I've got diabetes"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.04,
      "end_seconds": 212.74,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mhm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.19,
      "end_seconds": 216.02,
      "duration_seconds": 1.83,
      "text": "I've got low haemoglobin."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 217.57,
      "end_seconds": 219.53,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "and apart from that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.98,
      "end_seconds": 227.25,
      "duration_seconds": 6.27,
      "text": "Alright, diabetes and low haemoglobin, that matches what I have here. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.25,
      "end_seconds": 229.9,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No operations no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 230.76,
      "end_seconds": 236.44,
      "duration_seconds": 5.68,
      "text": "alright, have you had any palpitations, chest pain or coughing up blood?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 237.51,
      "end_seconds": 242.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.77,
      "text": "hmm, you know, none, as far as I know"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 248.13,
      "end_seconds": 251.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.5,
      "text": "did you get wheezing, fever or calf swelling?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 253.2,
      "end_seconds": 255.0,
      "duration_seconds": 1.8,
      "text": "No. None of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 258.79,
      "end_seconds": 263.76,
      "duration_seconds": 4.97,
      "text": "Alright, have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.81,
      "end_seconds": 267.97,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "No weakness or anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.01,
      "end_seconds": 271.88,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "first the numbers if you don't mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 281.03,
      "end_seconds": 283.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.54,
      "text": "Okay, give me a moment..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 300.7,
      "end_seconds": 316.82,
      "duration_seconds": 16.12,
      "text": "okay: SpO2 99 percent on room air, heart rate 86, blood pressure 116 over 73. Putting together what you've described, it points towards breathlessness with several possible contributors i'd also keep deconditioning in mind"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 317.91,
      "end_seconds": 321.21,
      "duration_seconds": 3.3,
      "text": "Should I be worried about this?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.76,
      "end_seconds": 334.54,
      "duration_seconds": 12.78,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's breathlessness with several possible contributors, and we'll know more once the an echocardiogram is back. Let's get an echocardiogram, for breathlessness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "CLINICAL_STAFF",
      "start_seconds": 335.67,
      "end_seconds": 338.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "the earliest is Friday 9 am"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 339.41,
      "end_seconds": 358.65,
      "duration_seconds": 19.24,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange a chest X-ray for breathlessness. A short daily walk building up slowly is a sensible start. A short walk every day even twenty minutes will help more than you'd think. Good. Let us know how you get on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 359.65,
      "end_seconds": 362.38,
      "duration_seconds": 2.73,
      "text": "nothing more from me, thanks"
    }
